  "goodToKnow": "Die Treuhand is a trust arrangement in law, where a Treuhänder (trustee) manages assets for others. In recent history, die Treuhand means the Treuhandanstalt (1990–1994), which privatised or closed around 8,500 East German state enterprises. Its work brought mass unemployment and remains controversial in the east; its head Detlev Rohwedder was murdered in 1991. Treuhänderisch means in trust. It has no plural."
